# NOTICE

Sourced from `https://github.com/MediaComem/FGDM4GS`
(WP2-WP3 work package, "Flat Geodata Models for Geoservices"), path
`WP2-WP3/model/<ModelDir>/<file>`:

- `IVS_V3.ili` (from `IVS_V2_1/`) - unmodified base model
- `Planungszonen_V2.ili` (from `Planungszonen_V1_1/`) - unmodified base model

The "_d" (data) derived models - `Axis_V1_1_d.ili` (from `Axis_V1_1/`),
`IVS_V3_d.ili` (from `IVS_V2_1/`), `Planungszonen_V2_d_A.ili` /
`Planungszonen_V2_d_B.ili` (from `Planungszonen_V1_1/`),
`SectoralPlanForRoadInfrastructure_V1_4_d.ili` (from
`SectoralPlanForRoadInfrastructure_V1_4/`) - started from the same repo
but their `VIEW` attribute names and dimensions have since been ALIGNED
to the actually published geoservice for each MGDM (ArcGIS REST `?f=json`
/ GetFeatureInfo for federal data), checked with
`scripts/crosscheck_view_attributes.py` (2026-08-29). `Axis_V1_1_d` and
`IVS_V3_d` now match `ch.astra.nationalstrassenachsen` /
`ch.astra.ivs-nat` field-for-field (bar the publication-added synthetic
`id` and the `_de/_fr/_it` language split of a `MultilingualText`, which
an INTERLIS VIEW cannot express). `SectoralPlanForRoadInfrastructure_V1_4_d`
gained a second VIEW (`view_spm`) for the `PlanningMeasure` half that the
published `ch.astra.sachplan-infrastruktur-strasse_kraft` layer
denormalises into the same wide table. `Planungszonen_V2_d_*` are
unchanged - no federal or geodienste service was found to check them
against.

These are derived models per the report's own methodology (chapter 4) -
each `IMPORTS` a real Swiss federal MGDM and defines a `VIEW`
(`PROJECTION OF`/`JOIN OF ... WHERE`) that flattens it for geoservice
publication. The companion "_gm" (graphic model) files in the
same repo are deliberately NOT vendored here - they add `StandardSymbology`
`GRAPHIC` definitions for cartographic representation, a separate concern
(backlog item 6, `.claude/PROGRESS.md`), not needed to exercise the VIEW
mapping itself.

The repo has no declared license (`license: null` via the GitHub API,
checked 2026-08-24). The report and this repo share an author
(`test@example.org`) with this project's own user - vendored
here as real, author-confirmed corpus material for testing VIEW
construction, not redistributed for any other purpose.

**Real corpus finding these fixtures exist to preserve** (2026-08-24):
all "_d" files exclusively use the `Name := expression` view attribute
redefinition form (`viewAttributes`'s `bare_redefinition_list`/
`modifier_reassignment` alternative) - NONE use `ALL OF`. This form was
previously `status: unresolved` in `InterlisModelBuilder` with "no real
corpus evidence" noted (backlog item 8 Lot A2) - these files are that
evidence. `View.RenamedBaseView`/`FormationKind`/`Where` and, since item
10, `View.ClassAttribute` all build correctly.

**To build these against their full IMPORTS closure**, a repo directory
also containing the base MGDMs they import is needed: `Axis_LV95_V1_1`
(`Axis_V1_1_d.ili`) and `BaseModel_SectoralPlans_LV95_V1_4`/
`BaseModel_SectoralPlans_Catalogues_V1_4`
(`SectoralPlanForRoadInfrastructure_V1_4_d.ili`) are both already present
in the real `ili_corpus/` scratch corpus (gitignored, re-fetched per
session - see `docs/model-resolution-strategy.md`) under their existing
files; `IVS_V3`/`Planungszonen_V2` are vendored directly alongside their
derived models here (the official `models.geo.admin.ch` catalog only has
the OLDER `IVS_V2_1`/`Planungszonen_V1_1` as of 2026-08-24 - the newer
versions these derived models target aren't published there yet, only in
the FGDM4GS repo itself).
